Description:
Tink is a multi-language, cross-platform, open-source cryptographic library
that provides cryptographic APIs that are secure, easy to use correctly, and
hard to misuse. In Chromium, it is used for standardized keyset serialization
and cryptographic agility (such as key rotation and algorithm transitions) on
top of BoringSSL.

